    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-42b898158423] and the linked PR [ev-1ea0042ea635] say that pod log search gains a match-case option, which is a new, additive feature. [ev-1f55d3277fc0] lists the changed files: the logs API (application.proto, swagger.json), the `argocd app logs` CLI command and its docs, and a new match-case toggle button in the UI pod-logs viewer. So the subject is a new case-sensitivity option for pod log search, exposed through the API, CLI and UI. The change is that the option was added. Nothing in the evidence says existing behaviour changes, so an environment whose operator does nothing is not affected. Confidence is low because the excerpts never name the exact request field or CLI flag, and they never say whether search was case-insensitive before.",
